# KEYS -- family: MORPH.
# Idea: the set is three whole patches and the pad blends them:
#   base   (bottom left)  ORGAN  drawbar organ on osc 1, held, bright, still
#   PLUCK  (X = 1)        a filtered pulse pluck on osc 2
#   BELL   (Y = 1)        an FM bell on osc 1, long ring, open filter
# Each macro morphs from the base toward its patch (model v2 "morph"); with
# both up, the pad mixes the two patches (top right: half pluck, half bell).
# X crossfades for real (the oscillator mix moves from osc 1 to osc 2, every
# envelope and filter value travels with it). One thing cannot crossfade:
# osc 1 is either the organ or the bell, so it switches at BELL = 0.5, where
# the other values are already halfway.
# audit: allow-jump BELL
# Feel if it works: the pad is a map with instruments at its corners and
# everything in between is playable; you find a spot you like and stay.
# Try: PLUCK on X, BELL on Y; play chords and sweep slowly around the pad.
voice lead
name KEYS
about "Organ, pluck and bell in one."
base release=30 osc2=puls intv=24 det=24 flt=lp ktrk=64 attack=0 fatk=0 drive=0 vib=0 lcut=0 lshp=0 fdcy=44
base wave=orgn mix=0 sus=110 decay=100 cutoff=100 env=8 reso=10 lvl=100 shape=92   # the organ

patch PLUCK mix=127 sus=0 decay=46 cutoff=58 env=72 reso=42 shape=36 lvl=116   # the pluck is short: lifted
patch BELL  wave=bell mix=0 sus=12 decay=98 release=84 cutoff=116 env=20 shape=72   # shape = the FM index

macro PLUCK "ORGAN" "PLUCK" "held drawbar organ .. pulse pluck"
  morph PLUCK

macro BELL "ORGAN" "BELL" "toward an FM bell; osc 1 switches at 0.5"
  morph BELL
